ffmpeg-dmo (10:9.0.2-dmo1+stereo3d9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Carry the six accepted multilayer and AC-3 fixes of the edition's FFmpeg
    fork (code.ffmpeg.org danielcamposramos/FFmpeg; not sent upstream, held by
    Daniel 2026-11-03), each as a fix patch and a separate test patch
    (0055 to 0066), ported from FFmpeg master to 9.0.2:
    - hevc-ps-layer-id-mask (0055, 0056): the HEVC VPS layer_id_included_flag
      bits are read in layer ID order (H.265 7.3.2.1, 7.4.3.1), so an MV-HEVC
      stream with layer IDs 0 and 6 keeps its second view.
    - hevc-parser-au-split (0057, 0058): the HEVC parser defers an access unit
      boundary until the next VCL NAL unit and follows the increasing layer
      order of H.265 F.7.4.2.4.4, so one 3D frame is no longer split across
      packets.
    - vvc-parser-layer1 (0059, 0060): the VVC parser assembles all picture
      units of an access unit, outputting the preceding access unit before a
      new one starts (H.266 7.4.2.4.3).
    - vvc-eos-recovery (0061, 0062): the VVC decoder keeps an end of sequence
      NAL unit of layer 0 for the access unit that follows it, so a CRA after
      EOS gets NoOutputBeforeRecoveryFlag (H.266 8.1.1, 7.4.3.11).
    - vvc-layer-au (0063, 0064): the VVC decoder keeps the base picture of a
      multilayer access unit, skipping unsupported layers, and reads only the
      layer 0 prefix SEI (H.266 D.2.2); it builds on vvc-parser-layer1.
    - ac3-parser-short-header (0065, 0066): the AC-3 and E-AC-3 sync scan
      reads only the seven byte header prefix again and leaves the metadata
      to a full header helper, which stops intermittent dropped E-AC-3 audio
      (eac3-5, eac3-core-bsf) and Valgrind's uninitialised reads.
  * The tests need samples that the FATE suite does not hold yet (hevc/mv-*,
    vvc/eos-cra, vvc/multilayer-sei, vvc/opi-missing-top-layer); the test
    commits of the fork say how they are generated.

  * Built with the Lean Code toolkit 0.1.25 of build-repo main 39663a5: the six
    build dependencies of the lc1 build now lead Build-Depends (they ended its
    folded field before); the plain source is otherwise the published one.

